    "content": "The Arizona Wildcats men’s basketball team has made four Final Four appearances in NCAA Tournament history: 1988, 1994, 1997, and 2001. All four appearances occurred under head coach Lute Olson, with the 1997 team winning the National Championship and the 2001 team finishing as runner-up. Arizona Final Four History: 1988: Lost in the semifinals to Oklahoma. 1994: Lost in the semifinals to Arkansas. 1997: Defeated Kentucky to win the National Championship. 2001: Defeated Michigan State in the semifinals, lost to Duke in the championship game. The program has not returned to the Final Four since 2001, despite numerous tournament appearances and multiple Elite Eight runs in the years following. This video explains why the 2024-25 season could be the year Arizona breaks their Final Four drought:09:51CBS Sports College BasketballYouTube• Jan 22, 2026 09:51",
